Maya (Presales): Need a 1-page POC cheat for tomorrow: streaming SDK (Node + Go), function/tool-call flow, structured JSON validation, handshake cURL, and a tiny security blurb (KMS + retention + SOC2 link). Can someone assemble quickly?

Raf (Eng): I can. Confirm hosted EU, ephemeral tokens required, and include a fallback to quantized model for cost spikes?

June (Sales): Yes EU. They want ephemeral creds sample and note that logs must be off by default. Finance will fill pricing placeholders.

Raf (Eng): Draft bullets + snippets:
- Goal: demo streaming chat with function calls and structured output validation.
- Env: hosted (eu), primary model: r-infer-2, fallback: r-infer-2-quant-small.
- Auth: API key or short-lived token (example token exchange omitted for brevity). TLS mandatory; KMS for keys. Logs not stored by default.

Node snippet:
```js
const c = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, region: 'eu' });
const s = c.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2' });
s.on('event', e => {
  if (e.type === 'function_call') fetch('https://hooks.customer/call', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(e.payload) });
  if (e.type === 'message') console.log(e.message);
});
```

Go snippet:
```go
cli := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_KEY"))
stream := cli.ChatStream(ctx, redwood.ChatParams{Model: "r-infer-2"})
for ev := range stream.Events() {
  if ev.Type == redwood.EventFunctionCall {
    http.Post("https://hooks.customer/call", "application/json", bytes.NewReader(ev.Payload))
  }
}
```

Handshake cURL:
```bash
curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_KEY" -H "Accept: text/event-stream" "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2&region=eu"
```

Structured output: validate against a small JSON Schema on receive, e.g. '{"type":"object","properties":{"intent":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"array"}}}'. Recommend using SDK schema hook for validation.

Operational knobs: batching window 10-25ms, KV prefix cache enabled. Fallback when queue latency >80ms or GPU queue >75% -> route to r-infer-2-quant-small.

Security blurb (short): EU-only endpoints; TLS in transit; KMS-managed keys at rest (HSM optional); logs off by default; SOC2 attestation link will be added by legal.

Troubleshooting quick hits: 401 -> check token/clock skew; SSE stalls -> missing Accept header/CORS; tool calls failing -> webhook TLS or IP block.

June (Sales): I'll chase finance/legal for pricing and SOC2 link. Tag me when final.

